Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a rounding that ends where the face between it and the next
stripe at its end vertex narrows to nothing rides on from there over the
corner patch at that stripe's other end and over that stripe's blend, and
the face at the end cuts it (mitcad#1926).

A U-shaped fin standing on a plate, its arms' tops sloping down into the
plate, inside the U a pit whose edges are rounded, the arms' inner feet
rounded with 1 and the arms' top edges with 0.5: at an inner arm end the
top's 0.5 (the rider B) and the foot's 1 (C) meet at the vertex where the
top, the arm's inner wall and the plate meet. The wall between them
narrows to nothing before that vertex: B's contact on the wall crosses the
contact of the corner patch (K) where C meets the pit's roundings. OCCT's
two-stripe corner failed there ("No intersection pc pc").

- PerformRideOnCornerAtEnd, tried before PerformTwoCorner for a corner of
  two stripes: where B's contact on the face between crosses the patch's
  contact at Q, B is cut at Q's section and walked on between its other
  face (its surface, run on past the face's edge) and the patch's surface
  as a support (RideOnCornerWalk), to the patch's end at C (J), then
  between that face and C's blend, to where its contact there comes down
  to C's contact with the face at the end (the walk stops at that bound of
  the support, P_foot).
- B's two new pieces have their side on the support on no face; the patch
  is split at Q's section and its piece towards C holds B's line on it, C
  holds B's other line from J to P_foot and ends in that point (its
  contact with the face at the end trimmed there), the curve the patch and
  C share is trimmed at J. B ends at the cut of its last piece by the face
  at the end, found section by section (ChFi3d_CutBySections, now shared:
  the cut is tangent to that face at P_foot), from P_top, where B's other
  contact meets that face, to P_foot.
- B's other contact runs on past the vertex: the edge of B's other face
  with the face at the end is prolonged from the vertex to P_top, on both
  faces (the other face grows up to it), and that face's edge with the
  face between, and the face between's edge with the face at the end, go
  (cut at the vertex).
- The stripes' points at Q, J and P_foot are made one once they are in
  the data structure (as a part ride's ends); B goes into it after the
  patch and C; a line shared against a stripe's way is turned
  (turnRidesAgainst); B's new pieces' faces are turned (the data structure
  orients their curves from their other side, their faces by the
  orientation found against the support).

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1727.

Failures (mitcad#1986): the guide's interpolation and the walk onto the
corner fail with OCCT's reports of a computation it cannot make
(ChFi3d_IsComputationFailure, 0016): the end does not ride on and is left
as before. Any other failure (a broken invariant, a signal) is rethrown.
